== K-UNIQ: the owner's two deals ==
  A-marginals: {0: Fraction(3, 4), 1: Fraction(1, 4)} / {0: Fraction(3, 4), 1: Fraction(1, 4)}; B predicts A: 1 / 3/4; relabellings of B mapping deal 1 to deal 2: 0 of 24
  [GREEN] K-UNIQ: equal A-marginals 3/4, prediction 1 vs 3/4, none of 24 relabellings connects them
  card encoding: deal 1 = {RRRB:1/4, RRBR:1/4, RBRR:1/4, BRRR:1/4}; equals E(RRRB): True; exchangeable: True
                 deal 2 = {RRRB:1/4, RRBR:1/4, RBRR:1/4, BRRB:1/4}; exchangeable: False (every base-theory preparation is a mixture of E(M))
  Pur-U detector on (deal 1, deal 2) with B-local slot permutations (S_3): connected = False
  [GREEN] K-UNIQ (card): deal 1 = E(RRRB); deal 2 not exchangeable, hence not preparable in the base theory; detector reports them unconnected

== K-SWAP2: the two-card swap core (av visible, a1 hidden): visible distribution is not the operational state ==
  W rank on filled arrangements (a1, av): read only = 2/4; read + swap = 4/4
  P1 = {(0, 0): Fraction(1, 2), (0, 1): Fraction(1, 2)}, P2 = {(1, 0): Fraction(1, 2), (1, 1): Fraction(1, 2)}: current visible distribution {0: Fraction(1, 2), 1: Fraction(1, 2)} vs {0: Fraction(1, 2), 1: Fraction(1, 2)}; after one swap P(av=0) = 1 vs 0
  engine: after shuffle 1 given v0=0 vs fresh deal: visible {0: Fraction(1, 2), 1: Fraction(1, 2)} vs {0: Fraction(1, 2), 1: Fraction(1, 2)}; after swap 2 P(av=0) = 1 vs 1/2
  [GREEN] K-SWAP2: equal current visible distributions, perfectly separated by a later swap; W(read)=2 < W(read+swap)=4

== K-HERALD (card analogue): destructive peek vs non-destructive peek of a1, deck {R,B}, a1 and b1 dealt ==
  peek outcome R: Pr = 1/2; post-state (a1, b1) = {('_', 'B'): '1'}
  peek outcome B: Pr = 1/2; post-state (a1, b1) = {('_', 'R'): '1'}
  ndp  outcome R: Pr = 1/2; post-state (a1, b1) = {('R', 'B'): '1'}
  ndp  outcome B: Pr = 1/2; post-state (a1, b1) = {('B', 'R'): '1'}
  [GREEN] K-HERALD (card): both reads reveal a1; peek leaves a1 empty in every branch, ndp leaves a1 = outcome in every branch

